|* Post-layout ro_ring5, ASSEMBLED: the four-ring wstv frequency ladder from
|* ONE flat `klt extract --parasitics` of each ring's own composed, DRC-clean
|* and LVS-clean GDS (layout/ro_ring5*/ro_ring5*.gds) -- real inter-gate metal
|* routing included, not the ideal wires sim/post-layout-ro-ring5/'s own
|* leaf-cell composition (layout/pex/ro_ring5_pex.spice: separate ro_nand2/
|* ro_stage extractions, wired together by the testbench itself) assumes
|* between gates.
|*
|* Purpose (issue #22, layout/README.md's "Newly possible, not yet done" note
|* under step 5). Every ring-level number recorded so far is either
|* pre-layout (design/*.spice, no physical interconnect at all) or a
|* leaf-cell post-layout composition (layout/pex/ro_ring5_pex.spice, five
|* separately-extracted cells wired by IDEAL testbench nets). Now that
|* layout/ro_ring5*/ exist as single composed, DRC/LVS-clean GDS files with
|* the inter-gate n1-n4/ro routing and vddr/vss rail busing actually drawn
|* (issue #22, PR #51), extracting THAT GDS directly for the first time
|* includes real inter-gate wiring in the ring's own period/swing/current
|* numbers -- a strictly better answer than the leaf-cell composition, per
|* layout/pex/README.md's own stated limitation.
|*
|* This deck is a two-way, same-corner comparison (assembled post-layout vs.
|* pre-layout control), NOT a three-way rerun against the leaf-cell
|* composition -- sim/bin/corner-run.py substitutes exactly one /Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/layout/pex-ring/ro_ring5_assembled_pex.spice
|* token, and adding a second templated library path is a runner change out
|* of this record's own scope. A reader wanting "how much did drawing the
|* real inter-gate wires cost, beyond the leaf composition's ideal-wire
|* assumption" compares THIS record's t_asm_* figures against
|* sim/post-layout-ro-ring5/'s own t_pex_* figures directly (both are
|* 125.0/1.98/ss-matched PVT points, just not the same ngspice
|* process) -- see sim/post-layout-ro-ring5-assembled/README.md.
|*
|* Topology. Four rings, each now a SINGLE subcircuit call (the composed GDS
|* IS design/xschem/ro_ring5.sch's own hierarchy, already wired) on its own
|* independent supply so each ring's own supply current stays separately
|* measurable:
|*
|*   r1..r4  POST-LAYOUT ASSEMBLED, wstv = 0.42 / 0.44 / 0.46 / 0.48 um --
|*           one physical, flat-extracted cell per ring, from
|*           layout/ro_ring5[_wstv0p4x]/ro_ring5*.gds via
|*           layout/pex-ring/pex.json + layout/bin/pex-netlist.py (shared,
|*           unmodified, with sim/post-layout-ro-ring5's own leaf-cell
|*           descriptor).
|*   q1..q4  PRE-LAYOUT control, the identical ladder from
|*           design/ro_array_core.spice's parameterized .subckt ro_ring5.
|*
|* Every ring drives its own output buffer -- ro_buf_pex (this library's own
|* copy, see layout/pex-ring/pex.json's _comment) for r1..r4, pre-layout
|* ro_buf for q1..q4 -- on one block supply per side, matching
|* sim/post-layout-ro-ring5's own buffering discipline (buffering ALL four
|* rings, not just one, is what makes the four periods a comparable ladder
|* rather than a mix of loaded/unloaded numbers -- see that slug's entry in
|* sim/README.md for the regression this avoids).
|*
|* The substrate tie. layout/pex-ring/ro_ring5_assembled_pex.spice declares
|* the extractor's substrate return node `vsubs` .global, same as
|* layout/pex/ro_ring5_pex.spice (klayout-tools#1503). This deck ties it HARD
|* to 0, the same physically-motivated choice sim/post-layout-ro-ring5's own
|* primary deck uses (every composed cell's own psub guard ring is tied to
|* vss, and vss is 0 here) -- inter-ring coupling through a floating
|* substrate is that slug's own separate question, not re-litigated here.
|*
|* PVT: the same four (temp, supply) points sim/post-layout-ro-ring5/ uses:
|*   -40 degC / 1.62 V   the measured entropy-binding corner (ss)
|*    27 degC / 1.80 V   nominal
|*   125 degC / 1.98 V   the worst five-stage ring swing in #10's grid
|*   -40 degC / 1.98 V   the fastest ring measured anywhere in that grid
|*
|* tstop/timestep match sim/post-layout-ro-ring5's own primary deck (160 ns,
|* 5p default 5p) -- the assembled ring's total R/C
|* (layout/pex-ring/pex.json's own build log: ~10.3-10.4 kOhm total series R,
|* ~42.2-42.3 fF total ground C per ring) is the same order of magnitude as
|* the leaf-cell composition's own per-cell totals summed, so no separate
|* re-derivation of the window was needed; confirmed by inspection of the
|* first run below rather than assumed.
|*
|* This file is a TEMPLATE: sim/bin/corner-run.py substitutes /Users/rwalters/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice,
|* ss, /Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/design/ro_array_core.spice, /Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/layout/pex-ring/ro_ring5_assembled_pex.spice, 125.0, 1.98 and 5p. As
|* committed it is not a runnable deck. Invoke with
|* `--ro-ring5 design/ro_array_core.spice` (for its ro_buf subckt, alongside
|* the ro_ring5 subckt design/ro_ring5.spice would also provide) and
|* `--pex-lib layout/pex-ring/ro_ring5_assembled_pex.spice`.
|
|.option scale=1u
|.lib "/Users/rwalters/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice" ss
|
|* pre-layout subcircuit library (ro_ring5 / ro_nand2 / ro_stage / ro_buf)
|.include "/Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/design/ro_array_core.spice"
|* post-layout ASSEMBLED subcircuit library (ro_ring5_assembled_pex_* +
|* its own ro_buf_pex), generated from layout/ro_ring5*/'s composed GDS
|.include "/Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/layout/pex-ring/ro_ring5_assembled_pex.spice"
|
|.temp 125.0
|
|* --- substrate return node: hard tie (see header) ----------------------
|Vsub vsubs 0 dc 0
|
|* --- post-layout ASSEMBLED rings, one flat-extracted cell per wstv -----
|Vddrr1 vddrr1 0 dc 1.98
|Venr1 enr1 0 dc 1.98
|xr1 enr1 r1o vddrr1 0 ro_ring5_assembled_pex_wstv0p42
|
|Vddrr2 vddrr2 0 dc 1.98
|Venr2 enr2 0 dc 1.98
|xr2 enr2 r2o vddrr2 0 ro_ring5_assembled_pex_wstv0p44
|
|Vddrr3 vddrr3 0 dc 1.98
|Venr3 enr3 0 dc 1.98
|xr3 enr3 r3o vddrr3 0 ro_ring5_assembled_pex_wstv0p46
|
|Vddrr4 vddrr4 0 dc 1.98
|Venr4 enr4 0 dc 1.98
|xr4 enr4 r4o vddrr4 0 ro_ring5_assembled_pex_wstv0p48
|
|* --- pre-layout control rings, identical topology, single-call subckt --
|Vddrq1 vddrq1 0 dc 1.98
|Venq1 enq1 0 dc 1.98
|xq1 enq1 q1o vddrq1 0 ro_ring5 wstv=0.42 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|
|Vddrq2 vddrq2 0 dc 1.98
|Venq2 enq2 0 dc 1.98
|xq2 enq2 q2o vddrq2 0 ro_ring5 wstv=0.44 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|
|Vddrq3 vddrq3 0 dc 1.98
|Venq3 enq3 0 dc 1.98
|xq3 enq3 q3o vddrq3 0 ro_ring5 wstv=0.46 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|
|Vddrq4 vddrq4 0 dc 1.98
|Venq4 enq4 0 dc 1.98
|xq4 enq4 q4o vddrq4 0 ro_ring5 wstv=0.48 lstv=2 cld=0.5f
|
|* --- output buffers: one per ring, on a block supply per side ----------
|Vddr vddr 0 dc 1.98
|xbr1 r1o r1ob vddr 0 ro_buf_pex
|xbr2 r2o r2ob vddr 0 ro_buf_pex
|xbr3 r3o r3ob vddr 0 ro_buf_pex
|xbr4 r4o r4ob vddr 0 ro_buf_pex
|Vddq vddq 0 dc 1.98
|xbq1 q1o q1ob vddq 0 ro_buf
|xbq2 q2o q2ob vddq 0 ro_buf
|xbq3 q3o q3ob vddq 0 ro_buf
|xbq4 q4o q4ob vddq 0 ro_buf
|
|.ic v(r1o)=0
|.ic v(r2o)=0
|.ic v(r3o)=0
|.ic v(r4o)=0
|.ic v(q1o)=0
|.ic v(q2o)=0
|.ic v(q3o)=0
|.ic v(q4o)=0
|
|* Limit the saved transient trace set to exactly what the .meas statements
|* below need. Without this, ngspice keeps a full-resolution voltage history
|* for every node in the deck -- including every per-terminal parasitic-star
|* leg node the flat ring extraction introduces beyond the leaf-cell
|* composition's own intra-cell-only nodes (see this file's header) -- and at
|* the ff corner's shorter, stiffer timesteps that history exhausted process
|* memory outright (`Error: memory required ... is more than memory
|* available`) rather than merely running slowly. None of those internal
|* leg voltages are read by any .meas below.
|.save v(r1o) v(r2o) v(r3o) v(r4o) v(r1ob)
|.save v(q1o) v(q2o) v(q3o) v(q4o) v(q1ob)
|.save i(Vddrr1) i(Vddrr4) i(Vddrq1) i(Vddrq4)
|
|.tran 5p 160n uic
|
|.control
|run
|
|* Period of every ring, from 8 whole periods with the first two rising
|* edges discarded as start-up -- the same estimator
|* sim/post-layout-ro-ring5/'s own primary deck uses, so the two campaigns'
|* periods are directly comparable across their shared PVT grid.
|meas tran tr1a when v(r1o)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran tr1b when v(r1o)=0.5*1.98 rise=11
|let t_asm_wstv0p42 = (tr1b - tr1a)/8
|meas tran tr2a when v(r2o)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran tr2b when v(r2o)=0.5*1.98 rise=11
|let t_asm_wstv0p44 = (tr2b - tr2a)/8
|meas tran tr3a when v(r3o)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran tr3b when v(r3o)=0.5*1.98 rise=11
|let t_asm_wstv0p46 = (tr3b - tr3a)/8
|meas tran tr4a when v(r4o)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran tr4b when v(r4o)=0.5*1.98 rise=11
|let t_asm_wstv0p48 = (tr4b - tr4a)/8
|
|meas tran tq1a when v(q1o)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran tq1b when v(q1o)=0.5*1.98 rise=11
|let t_pre_wstv0p42 = (tq1b - tq1a)/8
|meas tran tq2a when v(q2o)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran tq2b when v(q2o)=0.5*1.98 rise=11
|let t_pre_wstv0p44 = (tq2b - tq2a)/8
|meas tran tq3a when v(q3o)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran tq3b when v(q3o)=0.5*1.98 rise=11
|let t_pre_wstv0p46 = (tq3b - tq3a)/8
|meas tran tq4a when v(q4o)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran tq4b when v(q4o)=0.5*1.98 rise=11
|let t_pre_wstv0p48 = (tq4b - tq4a)/8
|
|* The headline ratio: same ring, same corner, real inter-gate wiring vs.
|* pre-layout (no interconnect at all).
|let slowdown_wstv0p42 = t_asm_wstv0p42 / t_pre_wstv0p42
|let slowdown_wstv0p44 = t_asm_wstv0p44 / t_pre_wstv0p44
|let slowdown_wstv0p46 = t_asm_wstv0p46 / t_pre_wstv0p46
|let slowdown_wstv0p48 = t_asm_wstv0p48 / t_pre_wstv0p48
|
|* Ladder span (DR-0003 section 8's skew_span, re-measured with real
|* inter-gate wiring). Stated as slowest/fastest ring under the ladder's
|* expected monotone ordering; the four periods above are printed
|* individually so a reader can confirm that ordering rather than take it on
|* trust.
|let skew_span_asm = t_asm_wstv0p42 / t_asm_wstv0p48
|let skew_span_pre = t_pre_wstv0p42 / t_pre_wstv0p48
|
|* Swing, ring node and buffered output, post-layout (assembled) vs.
|* pre-layout. Steady-state window: 20 ns of start-up discarded.
|meas tran vmaxr MAX v(r1o) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran vminr MIN v(r1o) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran vmaxrb MAX v(r1ob) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran vminrb MIN v(r1ob) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran vmaxq MAX v(q1o) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran vminq MIN v(q1o) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran vmaxqb MAX v(q1ob) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran vminqb MIN v(q1ob) from=20n to=160n
|let swing_frac_asm_ring = (vmaxr - vminr) / 1.98
|let swing_frac_asm_buf = (vmaxrb - vminrb) / 1.98
|let swing_frac_pre_ring = (vmaxq - vminq) / 1.98
|let swing_frac_pre_buf = (vmaxqb - vminqb) / 1.98
|
|* Per-ring supply current, running. i(Vsrc) is negative for current
|* delivered by the source, so the printed figures are sign-flipped to read
|* as consumed current.
|meas tran ir1raw AVG i(Vddrr1) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran ir4raw AVG i(Vddrr4) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran iq1raw AVG i(Vddrq1) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran iq4raw AVG i(Vddrq4) from=20n to=160n
|let i_asm_wstv0p42 = -ir1raw
|let i_asm_wstv0p48 = -ir4raw
|let i_pre_wstv0p42 = -iq1raw
|let i_pre_wstv0p48 = -iq4raw
|
|print t_asm_wstv0p42
|print t_asm_wstv0p44
|print t_asm_wstv0p46
|print t_asm_wstv0p48
|print t_pre_wstv0p42
|print t_pre_wstv0p44
|print t_pre_wstv0p46
|print t_pre_wstv0p48
|print slowdown_wstv0p42
|print slowdown_wstv0p44
|print slowdown_wstv0p46
|print slowdown_wstv0p48
|print skew_span_asm
|print skew_span_pre
|print swing_frac_asm_ring
|print swing_frac_asm_buf
|print swing_frac_pre_ring
|print swing_frac_pre_buf
|print i_asm_wstv0p42
|print i_asm_wstv0p48
|print i_pre_wstv0p42
|print i_pre_wstv0p48
|.endc
|.end
|

